(ned STORE RESULTS -- step 3 of the probing reset. Operator 2026-08-11:)
(this populates PB with the results, and clears all the tool lengths,)
(forcing the user to redo them all.)

(WHY CLEARING IS THE POINT, NOT A SIDE EFFECT. The whole chain exists for)
(when the setter has been bumped. Every stored tool length was measured)
(against where the setter USED TO BE, so the moment it moves they are all)
(wrong by the same unknown amount -- and a wrong length is silent: the)
(machine simply cuts at the wrong depth. Leaving them in place after a)
(recalibration would be the most dangerous possible outcome of a button)
(called STORE RESULTS. Wiping them makes the damage loud instead: every)
(tool reads zero until it has been re-measured.)

(IT CLEARS EXACTLY WHAT MEASURE ALL WILL RE-MEASURE -- the tools the rack)
(map says are in forks. Clearing a tool that is not in the rack would zero)
(something nobody is about to re-measure and nobody asked about.)

(REFUSES UNLESS ALL FOUR NUMBERS ARE PRESENT. Storing a half-finished)
(calibration and then wiping every length would leave the machine with no)
(lengths AND no way to measure them.)
o<cal_store_results> sub
  #<forks> = #1
  o1 if [#<forks> LE 0]
    #<forks> = 14
  o1 endif
  o5 if [#<_metric> EQ 0]
    (abort, STORE RESULTS: switch to MM first)
  o5 endif
  (a + b -- the setter position PB drives to)
  o10 if [#5181 EQ 0 AND #5182 EQ 0]
    (abort, STORE RESULTS: no probe XY in G30 - run FIND SHOULDER or SET PROBE HEIGHT first)
  o10 endif
  o11 if [#5183 EQ 0]
    (abort, STORE RESULTS: no probe height in G30 - run SET PROBE HEIGHT first)
  o11 endif
  (c -- the nose)
  o12 if [#3010 EQ 0]
    (abort, STORE RESULTS: no spindle nose height - run FIND SHOULDER first)
  o12 endif
  (d -- the plunge)
  o13 if [#3007 LE 0]
    (abort, STORE RESULTS: no plunge allowance - run SET PROBE HEIGHT first)
  o13 endif
  (PRINT, STORE RESULTS: PB has probe XY #5181 #5182, height #5183, nose #3010, plunge #3007 - all machine mm.)

  (THE WIPE IS THE CALLER'S JOB AND IT COVERS EVERY TOOL IN THE TABLE, not)
  (just the ones in forks. Operator 2026-08-11: "it has to zero ALL tools,)
  (and only probe the ones in the rack".)
  (The rack-only version bit immediately: T13 happened to be on the table)
  (when STORE RESULTS ran, so it kept a 129.8096 length measured against the)
  (OLD probe position -- and MEASURE ALL skips it too, because it is not in a)
  (fork. A stale length that nothing re-measures and nothing flags is the)
  (worst of the three states; zero is at least loud.)
  (Only the caller knows which tools exist, so only the caller can zero them)
  (all -- this file would have to guess a range and G10 L1 would invent the)
  (gaps as new entries.)
  (PRINT, STORE RESULTS: PB populated - every tool length zeroed by the caller. Fork tools get re-measured by MEASURE ALL; anything not in a fork stays at zero until it is done by hand.)
o<cal_store_results> endsub
M2 (end program)
